WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:18.559
sorry," a voice said.

2
00:00:18.579 --> 00:00:20.961
"I had to do it."

3
00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:23.183
"Who said that?"

4
00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.744
Daisy rubbed her neck.

5
00:00:25.745 --> 00:00:28.248
Her skin felt tingly from the bee sting.

6
00:00:32.108 --> 00:00:34.289
"Me." The bumblebee was hovering nearby.

7
00:00:34.309 --> 00:00:38.571
"I must be hearing imaginary voices," Daisy said.

8
00:00:38.591 --> 00:00:42.674
"I hope that doesn't mean I'm allergic to bee stings too!"

9
00:00:42.694 --> 00:00:44.735
"Don't be silly."

10
00:00:47.176 --> 00:00:48.897
The bumblebee buzzed in a circle.

11
00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:53.740
not imaginary.

12
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.521
I'm real, like you."

13
00:00:57.842 --> 00:00:58.642
Daisy blinked.

14
00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:01.704
She knew she shouldn't believe this was happening.

15
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.482
But she loved books and movies where people and animals could talk to each other.

16
00:01:07.163 --> 00:01:08.684
She wanted it to be true.

17
00:01:08.704 --> 00:01:11.225
"Okay, maybe this is real.

18
00:01:14.547 --> 00:01:18.209
If you can understand me, fly to the garden shed and back."

19
00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.571
The bee let out a tiny sigh.

20
00:01:21.591 --> 00:01:30.856
"We don't have time for games, I have to get you to Uh, I mean, okay, fine."

21
00:01:31.788 --> 00:01:33.530
The bee buzzed across the yard.

22
00:01:35.371 --> 00:01:38.694
She landed briefly on the garden shed and returned.

23
00:01:42.697 --> 00:01:43.538
Daisy cried.

24
00:01:43.558 --> 00:01:47.461
"So, can I understand all bees, or only you?"

25
00:01:47.481 --> 00:01:50.564
"Not just me, and not just bees.

26
00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.086
You can talk with all animals now."

27
00:01:54.427 --> 00:01:56.429
"What?" Daisy gasped.

28
00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.872
Just then a bird landed nearby.

29
00:02:01.312 --> 00:02:04.174
"I'm hungry," he sang.

30
00:02:04.194 --> 00:02:06.816
"So hungry!"

31
00:02:08.196 --> 00:02:08.997
Daisy grinned.

32
00:02:10.758 --> 00:02:12.399
She understood the bird too!

33
00:02:12.419 --> 00:02:16.582
"Mr. Smith has lots of bird feeders in his yard."

34
00:02:17.202 --> 00:02:19.003
Daisy pointed across the street.

35
00:02:19.924 --> 00:02:21.945
The bird looked at her in surprise.

36
00:02:21.965 --> 00:02:23.646
"Thank you!"

37
00:02:23.826 --> 00:02:24.287
He flew away.

38
00:02:30.328 --> 00:02:31.608
"This is amazing!"

39
00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:32.689
Daisy said.

40
00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:35.589
"I never thought I'd thank a bee for stinging me!

41
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:36.870
I'm Daisy.

42
00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:37.850
What's your name?"

43
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.031
The bee flapped her wings uncertainly.

44
00:02:41.051 --> 00:02:44.072
"Bees don't have names."

45
00:02:44.092 --> 00:02:47.333
"Hmm," Daisy said.

46
00:02:47.353 --> 00:02:51.274
"What if I call you Beatrice?"

47
00:02:51.294 --> 00:02:56.795
"Beatrice. That sounds like 'bee.'"

48
00:02:57.735 --> 00:02:59.256
The bee sounded pleased.

49
00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:01.196
"I like it!"

50
00:03:02.297 --> 00:03:04.118
"So, how did you do this, Beatrice?

51
00:03:04.598 --> 00:03:05.738
Are you a magic bee?"

52
00:03:06.779 --> 00:03:10.120
"Magic? Who told you there was magic?

53
00:03:11.421 --> 00:03:13.502
I never said anything about magic!"

54
00:03:14.042 --> 00:03:15.522
Beatrice sounded flustered.

55
00:03:15.542 --> 00:03:23.206
"Er, I shouldn't that is Excuse me, I'd better go check on my colony."

56
00:03:25.126 --> 00:03:28.568
"That was strange," Daisy thought as Beatrice left.

57
00:03:29.848 --> 00:03:32.330
"Daisy!" Kaleem ran toward her.

58
00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.733
"Kaleem! You'll never believe what just happened!"

59
00:03:36.113 --> 00:03:36.834
Daisy said.

60
00:03:36.854 --> 00:03:38.775
"You can tell me later."

61
00:03:39.376 --> 00:03:40.577
Kaleem looked worried.

62
00:03:40.597 --> 00:03:42.198
"Dumpling escaped!

63
00:03:42.678 --> 00:03:44.660
She must have sneaked out when I opened the door.

64
00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:48.423
The last time she got out, she didn't come home for two days."

65
00:03:52.346 --> 00:03:53.907
Dumpling was Kaleem's cat.

66
00:03:53.927 --> 00:03:58.311
"Don't worry, we'll find her," Daisy said.

67
00:03:58.331 --> 00:04:01.773
"It'll be easy, because I can talk to animals now."

68
00:04:02.874 --> 00:04:04.735
"What?" Kaleem frowned.

69
00:04:04.755 --> 00:04:07.057
"This is no time for weird jokes.

70
00:04:07.517 --> 00:04:07.997
Come on!

71
00:04:08.337 --> 00:04:09.798
I saw her run toward the forest."

72
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.062
Daisy followed as he hurried away.

73
00:04:17.343 --> 00:04:19.644
She tried to tell him about Beatrice again.

74
00:04:20.225 --> 00:04:22.546
But he still thought she was kidding around.

75
00:04:22.566 --> 00:04:24.848
"I'm telling the truth."

76
00:04:29.576 --> 00:04:31.838
Daisy spotted a squirrel up a tree.

77
00:04:31.858 --> 00:04:34.921
"Hey, squirrel, have you seen a cat out here?"

78
00:04:35.902 --> 00:04:37.083
The squirrel paused.

79
00:04:37.103 --> 00:04:39.645
"I smelled one.

80
00:04:40.205 --> 00:04:42.047
That's why I'm hiding up here."

81
00:04:43.108 --> 00:04:44.228
He scampered higher.

82
00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.072
Daisy told Kaleem what the squirrel had said.

83
00:04:49.092 --> 00:04:50.654
"Stop it!"

84
00:04:51.114 --> 00:04:53.076
Kaleem sounded even more annoyed.

85
00:04:53.096 --> 00:04:55.097
"We have to find Dumpling!"

86
00:04:56.238 --> 00:04:57.900
"I know where your cat is!"

87
00:04:58.409 --> 00:04:59.713
a tiny voice squeaked.
